 '5. **@types/nodemailer 8.0.2 sits beside nodemailer 10, which ships its OWN declarations (READ + MEASURED layout):** 10.0.0 migrated to TypeScript, `"type": "module"`, exports map import -> dist/esm, require -> dist/cjs; the CJS entry exports createTransport both directly and on `.default` (`__esModule` true). Which declarations tsc picks for `import nodemailer from \'nodemailer\'` / `nodemailer.Transporter` is unmeasured — the gate\'s tsc per service decides it.',
 '6. **The only 9 -> 10 BREAKING CHANGE listed is "Node.js 20 or newer is required" (READ, CHANGELOG.md of the installed 10.0.12)** — the services run node:24-alpine (auth Dockerfile READ) and the host v24.7.0. Both call sites are byte-identical base -> head; both option shapes built on 10.0.12 (MEASURED, streamTransport / no connection). No real SMTP exchange was driven.',
 '7. **The mandated body carries `Refs KS-729` although the commit message does not (READ):** the PR body has both Refs lines and Linear links both as `contributes`; the commit message carries only `Refs KS-1378`. The merger composes. The audit tool prints the CLEANUP rows with KS-470 / KS-729 HYPHENATED (leg6.out) — quoting them verbatim in the squash body would attach KS-470 (Done, archived): a foreign key.',
 '8. **The audit fuse (READ, handover + READY):** "the audit fuse — 21.9 h, computed 2026-09-29T02:08Z" — after 2026-09-30T00:00Z every Blockchain/Dev push and merge is refused unless Kam\'s own DKIM mail reaches secuura-blockchain@. A GO issued after it may not be mergeable. Not this PR\'s defect; Kam\'s clock.',
 '9. **The six HELD `-b43-` branches (READ, handover):** KS-1371 / KS-1359 / KS-1369 / KS-1360 / KS-1375 / KS-1054 committed, NOT pushed, all waiting for #1339 to merge. The WIDEN census refuses the launch (rc 15) if any is opened as a PR first — as intended; the successor must not push them before this gate launches.',
 '10. **GitHub mergeable_state `unstable`** (gh_read_1.out) — mergeable True; not measured further (Actions are retired; no claim either way).',
 '11. **Two push logs exist; the READY cites the second (READ):** the seat\'s first push returned RC 1 with nothing pushed; push1378.out ends `RC=0` and the branch is at origin (ls-remote). The push log is in the seat\'s SESSION SCRATCHPAD, not its record folder — it can vanish on a reboot; the capture holds its STOP counts and its last 40 lines.', '',
